---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionRail from '../components/SectionRail.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ReasoningBoard from '../components/ReasoningBoard.astro';
import { tools } from '../data/site';
const rail=[{id:'engineering-intro',title:'Intro'},{id:'how-i-build',target:'how-i-build-runway',title:'How I Build'},{id:'mobile',title:'Mobile'},{id:'backend',title:'Backend'},{id:'systems',title:'Systems'},{id:'media',title:'Media / Local Software'},{id:'ai-assisted',title:'AI-assisted'},{id:'workbench',title:'Workbench'}];
const domains=[
  {id:'mobile',number:'01',title:'Mobile',copy:'Mobile work is a product boundary as much as a platform choice. I work through application architecture, user-facing state, local persistence, background work, device capabilities, permission boundaries, and offline behavior.',points:['Android application architecture','Jetpack Compose and user-facing state','Local persistence and background scheduling','Permission minimization and device boundaries'],example:"IT’S SO OVER is a useful example of Android product boundaries: permissioned device signals become behavioral context on-device, while the product remains useful without a behavioral backend or runtime AI dependency. The difficult part is not collecting more data. It is extracting only the context that meaningfully changes product behavior while keeping permissions, privacy, and interruption under control."},
  {id:'backend',number:'02',title:'Backend',copy:'Backend systems carry contracts, persistence, state ownership, asynchronous workflows, authentication, failure boundaries, and the evidence needed to understand them in production.',points:['Java and Spring Boot','PostgreSQL, Redis, and Flyway','Streaming and SSE','API contracts, failures, and observability'],example:'OrchestrAI explored provider and model orchestration through a production-minded backend. The product was archived, but the work remains a useful example of clear provider boundaries, streaming, persistence, and deliberate failure behavior.'},
  {id:'systems',number:'03',title:'Systems',copy:'Local software and background services need explicit ownership of processes, resources, lifecycle, recovery, and failure. Linux is part of the product surface when the work lives on the user’s machine.',points:['Linux and Rust','Process orchestration and systemd','Resource-aware execution','Background services and recovery'],example:'GeoCall is a small example: local scheduling, SQLite, and systemd turn a repeated manual check into a focused private automation without pretending it is a larger product.'},
  {id:'media',number:'04',title:'Media / Local Software',copy:'Media systems make resource constraints and long-running operations impossible to ignore. Non-destructive state, local processing, progress, cancellation, and deterministic execution matter because the user’s source material matters.',points:['FFmpeg and local processing','Non-destructive project state','Long-running operations','Desktop and resource constraints'],example:'EDIP uses AI to understand editorial intent, while validated plans become deterministic local media operations. The interesting problem is not merely using AI; it is making revision understandable and execution dependable.'},
  {id:'ai-assisted',number:'05',title:'AI-assisted systems',copy:'AI is one mechanism among others. LLM APIs, provider and model orchestration, and tools such as Codex, Claude, and Gemini can accelerate investigation and implementation, but they do not replace product judgement.',points:['LLM APIs','Provider and model orchestration','AI-assisted engineering workflows','Judgement remains accountable'],example:'The question stays the same: does the mechanism improve the product, preserve clear boundaries, and give the person using it a result they can understand and control?'},
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Engineering | Mehmet Arslanca" description="How Mehmet Arslanca thinks about software across product reasoning, mobile, backend, systems, local media, and AI-assisted workflows.">
  <SectionRail sections={rail}/>
  <PageHero id="engineering-intro" label="Engineering" title="Problems dictate the architecture, not my comfort zone." statement="These are the areas I move through when the product needs them." image="/images/page-heroes/engineering.png" />
  <section id="how-i-build" class="section container build-intro" data-section-anchor aria-labelledby="build-heading"><div data-scroll-reveal><p class="label">How I Build</p><h2 id="build-heading">From problem<br/>to evidence.</h2><p>Decisions become technical only after the product has given them a reason to.</p></div></section>
  <ReasoningBoard/>
  <section class="section container principles"><div data-scroll-reveal><p class="label">Working principles</p><h2>Complexity has to earn its place.</h2></div><ul data-scroll-reveal><li>Unknowns stay visible until evidence resolves them.</li><li>Reversible decisions remain reversible.</li><li>Architecture protects product behavior.</li><li>Technology stays subordinate to the problem.</li></ul></section>
  <div class="domains">{domains.map((domain)=><section id={domain.id} class="section container domain" data-section-anchor aria-labelledby={`${domain.id}-heading`}><div class="domain-title" data-scroll-reveal><span class="label">{domain.number}</span><h2 id={`${domain.id}-heading`}>{domain.title}</h2></div><div class="domain-copy" data-scroll-reveal data-motion-lag=".03"><p class="lead">{domain.copy}</p><ul>{domain.points.map((point)=><li>{point}</li>)}</ul><p class="example"><span class="label">Project example</span>{domain.example}</p>{domain.id==='media'&&<a class="text-link" href="/products/edip/">Explore EDIP <span class="arrow">→</span></a>}{domain.id==='mobile'&&<a class="text-link" href="/products/#its-so-over">See IT’S SO OVER <span class="arrow">→</span></a>}</div></section>)}</div>
  <section id="workbench" class="section container workbench" data-section-anchor aria-labelledby="workbench-heading"><div class="workbench-heading" data-scroll-reveal><div><p class="label">Tools & Environment</p><h2 id="workbench-heading">Workbench</h2></div><p>The languages, systems, tools, and machine I actually work with.</p></div><div class="workbench-grid">{tools.map((group,index)=><article class="workbench-group" data-scroll-reveal data-motion-lag={String(index*.01)}><span class="label">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{group.title}</h3><ul>{group.items.map((item)=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></article>)}</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .build-intro>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.55fr 1.45fr;gap:4rem 8rem}.build-intro h2{font-size:clamp(4rem,9vw,9rem);line-height:.88}.build-intro div>p:last-child{grid-column:2;max-width:45ch;color:var(--text-muted)}.principles{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem 8rem;padding-inline:clamp(2rem,7vw,7rem);background:var(--bg-elevated)}.principles h2{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,5rem);margin-top:1rem}.principles ul,.domain-copy ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.principles li,.domain-copy li{padding-block:.6rem;color:var(--text-muted)}.domain{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.75fr 1.25fr;gap:4rem 10rem;min-height:80svh;align-items:center}.domain-title{display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.5rem 1fr;gap:1rem}.domain-title h2{font-size:clamp(3.5rem,7vw,7rem);line-height:.9}.domain-copy{max-width:60ch}.domain-copy .lead{max-width:58ch;font-family:var(--font-body);font-size:1.0625rem;font-weight:400;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-muted)}.example{margin:2.5rem 0;color:var(--text-muted)}.example span{display:block;margin-bottom:.75rem}.workbench-heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.65fr 1.35fr;gap:4rem 8rem;align-items:end;margin-bottom:5rem}.workbench-heading h2{font-size:clamp(4rem,8vw,8rem)}.workbench-heading>p{max-width:42ch;color:var(--text-muted)}.workbench-grid{display:grid;row-gap:clamp(4rem,7vw,7rem)}.workbench-group{width:min(48%,36rem);display:grid;grid-template-columns:2.5rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem 1.25rem;align-items:baseline}.workbench-group:nth-child(odd){justify-self:start}.workbench-group:nth-child(even){justify-self:end;width:min(45%,34rem);margin-right:clamp(0rem,4vw,4rem)}.workbench-group:nth-child(4n+3){margin-left:clamp(1rem,5vw,5rem)}.workbench-group h3{font-size:clamp(1.65rem,2.6vw,2.65rem)}.workbench-group ul{grid-column:2;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;font-family:var(--font-mono);color:var(--text-muted);font-size:.68rem;line-height:1.8}
  @media(max-width:900px){.domain,.principles,.build-intro>div,.workbench-heading{grid-template-columns:1fr}.domain{min-height:0}.build-intro div>p:last-child{grid-column:auto}.workbench-group{width:min(58%,32rem)}.workbench-group:nth-child(even){width:min(55%,30rem);margin-right:0}}@media(max-width:600px){.workbench-group,.workbench-group:nth-child(even){width:100%;margin:0;grid-template-columns:2rem 1fr}.workbench-group:nth-child(4n+3){margin-left:0}}
</style>
